# Privacy Policy — NotePin Chrome Extension

**Last updated: May 2026**

## Summary
NotePin does **not** collect, transmit, sell, or share any user data.
All notes are stored **only on your own device**.

## What data is stored?
- The notes you write
- Your theme preference (light / dark / auto)

These are saved using Chrome's built-in `chrome.storage.local` API, which keeps
data on your computer only. Nothing is uploaded to any server.

## What data is NOT collected?
- ❌ No personal information
- ❌ No browsing history
- ❌ No analytics or tracking
- ❌ No cookies
- ❌ No third-party services
- ❌ No account or login required
- ❌ No internet connection used

## Permissions explained
| Permission | Why we need it |
|------------|---------------|
| `activeTab` | To read the URL of the tab you're on (only when you click the icon) so the right note can be loaded for that website. |
| `storage`   | To save your notes locally on your device. |

## What happens if I uninstall?
All your notes are automatically deleted when you uninstall the extension.

## Changes to this policy
Any updates will be posted at the same URL with a new "Last updated" date.

## Contact
For questions, please open an issue on the extension's GitHub page.
